{"name":"Blue Bikini","hex":"#00bbee","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"blue","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a blue hue.","Depressed, melancholic, sad."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The colour of the clear sky or the deep sea; the colour midway between green and violet in the visible spectrum and one of the primary additive colours.","Anything coloured blue, especially to distinguish it from similar objects differing only in colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blue"},{"term":"bikini","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A brief, often minimalistic two-piece bathing suit worn by women, especially one that exposes the midriff and navel.","A brief bathing suit covering only the pelvis (equivalent to the bottom portion of a two-piece bikini), worn by any gender."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bikini"}],"entries":[{"title":"Bikini","blocks":[{"text":"A bikini is a women's two-piece swimsuit featuring a top piece covering the breasts, and a bottom piece covering the pelvis and some or all of the buttocks. The extent covered by both pieces can vary, from those that offer full coverage of the breasts, pelvis, and buttocks, to more revealing designs with thong or G-string bottoms that cover only the mons pubis and intergluteal cleft, and tops that cover only the areolae. Bikini bottoms covering about half of the buttocks may be described as \"Brazilian-cut\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/03/Three_Girls_Surfers_Paradise_in_bikinis.jpg/330px-Three_Girls_Surfers_Paradise_in_bikinis.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bikini","wikidata":"Q14090"},{"title":"Blue","blocks":[{"text":"Blue is one of the three primary colours in the RGB (additive) colour model, as well as in the RYB colour model. It lies between violet and cyan on the spectrum of visible light. The term blue generally describes colours perceived by humans observing light with a dominant wavelength between approximately 450 and 495 nanometres. The clear daytime sky and the deep sea appear blue because of an optical effect known as Rayleigh scattering. An optical effect called the Tyndall effect explains blue eyes. Distant objects appear more blue because of another optical effect called aerial perspective."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg/330px-Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue","wikidata":"Q1088"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f4/Able_crossroads.jpg/500px-Able_crossroads.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f4/Able_crossroads.jpg/1280px-Able_crossroads.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f4/Able_crossroads.jpg/500px-Able_crossroads.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Operation Crossroads was a nuclear test series at the Bikini Atoll, and the inspiration for the naming of two French swimsuit designs at the time, including the bikini.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAble_crossroads.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/66/Villa_Romana_del_Casale_BW_2025-04-28_11-11-12.jpg/500px-Villa_Romana_del_Casale_BW_2025-04-28_11-11-12.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/66/Villa_Romana_del_Casale_BW_2025-04-28_11-11-12.jpg/1280px-Villa_Romana_del_Casale_BW_2025-04-28_11-11-12.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/66/Villa_Romana_del_Casale_BW_2025-04-28_11-11-12.jpg/500px-Villa_Romana_del_Casale_BW_2025-04-28_11-11-12.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The ancient Roman Villa Romana del Casale (286–305 CE) in Sicily has one of the earliest known bikini-type images.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AVilla_Romana_del_Casale_BW_2025-04-28_11-11-12.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6f/Bathing_Beauties_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Bathing_Beauties_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6f/Bathing_Beauties_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Bathing_Beauties_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABathing_Beauties_(cropped).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/86/AKellermanUnitard1909.JPG/500px-AKellermanUnitard1909.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/86/AKellermanUnitard1909.JPG/500px-AKellermanUnitard1909.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAKellermanUnitard1909.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3f/Jane_Wyman%2C1935_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-Jane_Wyman%2C1935_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3f/Jane_Wyman%2C1935_%28cropped%29.jpg/1280px-Jane_Wyman%2C1935_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3f/Jane_Wyman%2C1935_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-Jane_Wyman%2C1935_%28cropped%29.